Minecraft FIGfont (phm-minecraft.flf) by Philippe Majerus (www.phm.lu)
This font uses two rows of Unicode 16.0 octant characters to render the
pixelated characters from the Minecraft game by Mojang.
Some characters widths are slightly adjusted, such as ()*<>@fkl{}~ to fix
the required even number of pixels columns required by octants, and in
heights to fit in two rows.
Date: January 9, 2026

